$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=twinsv  LOC_AFTER=?

* The twin-type sieve upper bound: there are absolute constants C and t0 such that for every m and every t at least t0 the number of primes q up to t with m q + 1 prime is at most C ( m / phi m ) squared times t over the square of the logarithm of t.

